		{
			description: [
				"Supplementaries and Amendments improve familiar Minecraft blocks with useful interactions and decorative variants. JEI is the safest way to discover them."
				"Amendments changes how familiar blocks can be placed: lanterns and other objects may hang, sit, or attach to walls according to the face clicked. Test orientation on a workshop wall before repeating it through a build."
				"Supplementaries mixes decoration with utility. Notice boards communicate, jars display or hold supported contents, signposts mark routes, and redstone-aware objects can make a settlement feel physically connected to its systems."
				"Start with silhouette and purpose, then choose a small palette, then add depth. Furniture and detail blocks work best when they explain how a room is used instead of covering every empty surface."
			]
			id: "02D6AD5207DB9BAB"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7816B27B34AC8D6D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 15
