		{
			dependencies: ["02D6AD5207DB9BAB"]
			description: [
				"Rechiseled turns one material into many coordinated textures. Use its chisel and keep strong patterns for trims, floors or feature walls."
				"Rechiseled supplies coordinated texture families; FramedBlocks supplies unusual shapes that borrow another block's appearance. Decide texture first and geometry second so an accent does not turn into visual noise."
				"Start with silhouette and purpose, then choose a small palette, then add depth. Furniture and detail blocks work best when they explain how a room is used instead of covering every empty surface."
				"Once the method works, label its inputs, outputs, controls, route, or habitat in plain language and show one teammate. Shared documentation turns a completed quest into knowledge that remains useful when the original player is offline."
