		{
			description: [
				"First establish the silhouette, then choose a small block palette, then add depth with frames, roofs, windows and supports. Detail cannot rescue a shape that does not work from a distance."
				"Repeat a few motifs so the settlement feels related: the same roof pitch, foundation material, lantern style or window rhythm can link very different buildings."
				"Handcrafted, Another Furniture, Supplementaries and the decoration mods are strongest when they finish a room with a purpose instead of filling every empty block."
				"Start with silhouette and purpose, then choose a small palette, then add depth. Furniture and detail blocks work best when they explain how a room is used instead of covering every empty surface."
			]
