		{
			dependencies: ["1FF3A7AE02B1761E"]
			description: [
				"Amendments and related decoration mods add contextual variants. A lantern, sign or small object may hang, sit or attach differently depending on the face and angle used for placement."
				"Test unfamiliar decorative blocks in a workshop wall before using them across an entire build. If a variant looks wrong, break it and try another face or orientation rather than assuming the texture is broken."
				"These tiny physical rules are part of the pack's visual language: objects should look supported by the world around them."
				"Amendments changes how familiar blocks can be placed: lanterns and other objects may hang, sit, or attach to walls according to the face clicked. Test orientation on a workshop wall before repeating it through a build."
			]
			id: "26693C1DC7FB0C9C"
			rewards: [{
				id: "43EE0E8C137FB52F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
