		}
		{
			description: [
				"Construct a small workshop wall with floor, ceiling, fence, slab, stair, and full-block faces. Place vanilla and modded lanterns, signs, shelves, ropes, and similar objects against every sensible surface."
				"Amendments and Supplementaries can supply contextual variants such as wall-mounted or hanging forms. The face clicked, support block, sneaking state, or interaction order may change the result even when the item name looks familiar."
				"This is why a soul lantern can become a better-looking wall or hanging variant on this server. Preserve the behaviour, record the placement gesture, and use the wall as the settlement's permanent sample catalogue."
			]
			id: "1C89C8BFA7B44BF7"
			rewards: [{
				id: "37A799A6FADF0580"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Learn placement variants before they surprise the build"
			tasks: [{
